## Job Terms

### Elevations

A glazed opening. Is not intended to include surrounding conditions like structural members, brake metal, etc.

Also known as: 
    * typical elevation 
    * glazed opening 
    * framed opening 

#### Drawing Elevations

The process of setting rules and conditions needed to match the typical elevations of an architectural set.

Also known as: configuring, building out

#### Panels


#### Standard Elevation

A catch-all term for glazed openings without a specified type of framing system (curtain wall, window wall, storefront, etc). 

#### Punched Entrance

A simply framed door without sidelites.

### Entrance

The combination of a door frame and a door leaf.

### Glass Product

A glass fabrication to be applied to panels in an elevation.

Also known as: glass type, glass fab



